course: dictionary
lesson: 13262
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Gloss is one of these words. «The new car had a gloss that shone in the sun.» Here gloss means a smooth shine on a surface.
explain: «She read the gloss at the back of the book to find out what the hard word meant.» Now gloss means a short explanation of a word. The clues are read, meant and hard word. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Gloss can also be a verb. «He tried to gloss over the broken window.» To gloss over a problem means to talk about it quickly so people do not notice it. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Gloss can mean a smooth shine on a surface.
fact: «Gloss paint» is shiny paint used on doors and wood.
fact: «Lip gloss» is a make-up product that makes lips shiny.
fact: A gloss is a short explanation of a word, often written in the margin or in a glossary.
fact: «Gloss over» means to talk about a problem quickly so people do not notice it.
exercise: «The table had a high gloss that reflected the lamp.» What does gloss mean here? | A sweet, sticky food | A dull, rough surface | A short explanation of a word | *A smooth shine on a surface
exercise: «Check the gloss at the back of the book if you do not know a word.» What is a gloss here? | *A short explanation of a hard word | A picture of a fish | A loud noise in the night | A shiny lip product
exercise: «The teacher tried to gloss over the mistake.» What does gloss over mean? | *To talk about a problem quickly so people do not notice it | To polish the floor until it shines | To explain a word in the margin | To read very slowly
test: Lip gloss is a make-up product. What is it used for? | To make hair curly | *To make lips shiny | To stop the rain | To keep feet warm
test: «The gloss paint on the door was bright red.» What is gloss paint? | A thin paper for drawing | *Shiny paint used on doors and wood | A type of cake | Water used to clean windows
exam: In «Her gloss explained the hard word, so I understood it.» what is a gloss? | A loud cheer | A shiny car | *A short explanation of a word | A smell of flowers
